window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-685427f63cb423d3"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"add-mac-telemetry\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"mac\">为 Mac 添加遥测日志</h1> <p>使用 Codex 为一个 Mac 功能加入 Logger、运行应用，并从统一日志中验证操作是否发生。</p> <p>使用 Codex 和 Build macOS Apps 插件，在窗口、侧边栏、命令或同步流程周围添加少量高信号 <code>Logger</code> 事件；随后运行应用，并通过 Console 或 <code>log stream</code> 证明相应操作确实触发。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要可靠追踪窗口打开、侧边栏选择、菜单命令、菜单栏操作、同步里程碑或回退路径的 Mac 应用功能。</li> <li>Codex 应在修改代码后重新运行应用、查看日志，并依据证据而不是猜测来决定下一步修复的代理式调试循环。</li> <li>本地应用会话采集流程：希望记录紧凑的用户操作序列和应用生命周期事件，并在重复运行之间进行比较。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-macos-apps（需联网）</a></td> <td>使用 macOS 遥测与构建/运行技能添加结构化 <code>OSLog</code> 埋点、启动应用、操作界面路径，并通过 Console 或 <code>log stream</code> 验证产生的事件。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>应用日志</td> <td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/os/logger\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OSLog Logger（需联网）</a></td> <td>结构化的统一日志能为 Codex 提供范围明确、易于筛选的反馈循环，不会让代码库充斥 <code>print</code> 语句。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>代理工作流</td> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build macOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a></td> <td>该插件中的遥测与构建/运行技能就是为协同工作设计的：为一个流程埋点、启动应用、检查日志，再精简事件集合。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>运行时验证</td> <td>Console.app 和 <code>log stream --predicate ...</code></td> <td>具体的日志筛选条件和样例输出能让代理更容易交接工作，并使新的埋点在不同运行中都易于验证。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>为一个功能加入埋点并从日志验证</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 Build macOS Apps 插件，为 [name one Mac feature or action flow] 添加轻量级统一日志，然后运行应用，并从日志中验证这些事件是否按预期顺序发生。\n\n约束：\n- 优先使用 `Logger`（来自 `OSLog`），不要用 `print`；为此功能设置清楚的 subsystem/category（子系统/类别）组合，方便筛选日志。\n- 在每个重要操作边界或状态转换处记录一行简短日志，例如窗口打开、侧边栏选中项改变、菜单命令调用、同步开始、同步完成或进入回退路径。\n- 保持永久保留的 `info` 日志稳定且信息明确。只对嘈杂的本地细节使用 `debug`；任务结束前可移除或降低临时日志级别。\n- 不要记录机密、身份验证令牌、个人数据或原始文档内容。如果必须记录标识符，应选择风险最低的隐私注解，并说明原因。\n- 构建并运行应用，操作被埋点的流程；准确提供所用的 Console 筛选器或 `log stream` predicate，以及一两条代表性日志。\n- 如果流程很长、时有时无，或更适合手动复现，可以把筛选后的日志流保存为小型本地会话跟踪文件；必要时让我手动操作，再读回该文件并总结事件时间线。\n- 如果预期事件没有出现，就把日志放到最可能出问题的控件路径附近，重新运行流程，直到日志能解释实际发生的情况。\n\n交付：\n- 新的 logger 设置和添加的确切事件\n- 使用的 Console 筛选器或 `log stream` predicate\n- 简短说明这些日志现在比以前多暴露了什么\n- 如果进行了较长时间的采集，提供保存的跟踪文件和时间线摘要\n- 一两条能证明该流程已正确埋点的代表性日志\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build macOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">代理技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"add-one-logger-where-debugging-gets-vague\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"logger\">在调试变得含糊的地方添加 Logger</h2> <p>本用例适用于这样的 Mac 应用流程：仅说“发生了某件事”太含糊，仅凭代码审阅无法排查。可以让 Codex 围绕一种行为添加少量高信号统一日志、运行应用、触发该行为，再从 Console 或 <code>log stream</code> 确认预期事件确实发生。</p> <p>使用 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build macOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a>来完成这一循环。其 macOS 遥测技能刻意保持轻量：使用 Apple 的 <code>Logger</code>，选择清楚的 subsystem/category（子系统/类别）组合，记录操作边界和状态转换，避免敏感载荷；在本地构建并运行后验证事件，而不是假定埋点已正确接线。</p> <p><a id=\"why-telemetry-is-useful-for-agentic-engineering\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">遥测为何有助于代理式工程</h2> <p>良好的日志能让 Codex 在每次补丁后运行可重复的反馈循环。代理无需让你手动检查每个窗口、菜单操作或同步转换；它可以运行应用、操作相应流程、查看筛选后的日志，再根据证据决定下一处代码改动。</p> <p>这对三种代理循环尤其有帮助：</p> <ul> <li><strong>免手动调试循环：</strong> Codex 为可疑流程加入埋点、启动应用、点击侧边栏或触发命令、读取输出的日志序列、修复状态更新路径，然后重复同一流程，直到日志与界面行为一致。</li> <li><strong>应用会话采集循环：</strong> Codex 为应用启动、窗口打开、侧边栏选中项改变、导入开始、导入完成和导入失败分别添加一个事件；然后运行一次本地会话并总结时间线，让缺失或顺序错误的状态转换一目了然。</li> <li><strong>人工驱动采集循环：</strong> Codex 启动带有日志功能的应用，并在你手动操作复杂流程时保持筛选后的日志流运行；随后检查采集到的会话，并根据跟踪结果提出下一项修复。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"keep-the-instrumentation-small-and-filterable\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">让埋点保持精简并便于筛选</h2> <p>请 Codex 为每个功能区域创建一个 logger，而不是为每次状态变化都永久记录一行日志。使用 <code>Windowing</code>、<code>Commands</code>、<code>MenuBar</code>、<code>Sidebar</code>、<code>Sync</code> 或 <code>Import</code> 这类功能类别，会让下一次筛选日志容易得多。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-swift\">import OSLog\n\nprivate let logger = Logger(\n  subsystem: Bundle.main.bundleIdentifier ?? \"SampleApp\",\n  category: \"Sidebar\"\n)\n\n@MainActor\nfunc selectItem(_ item: SidebarItem) {\n  logger.info(\"Selected sidebar item: \\(item.id, privacy: .public)\")\n  selection = item.id\n}\n</code></pre> <p>对长期有用的简短操作与生命周期事件使用 <code>info</code>；对更嘈杂的本地状态细节使用 <code>debug</code>，并考虑在任务结束前移除这些细节或降低日志级别。只有在测量某段耗时区间时才添加 signpost，不要默认添加。</p> <p><a id=\"ask-codex-to-prove-the-event-from-logs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">要求 Codex 用日志证明事件确实发生</h2> <p>有价值的不只是添加 <code>Logger</code> 调用。还要让 Codex 运行应用、触发已埋点的流程，并提供实际使用的 Console 筛选条件或 <code>log stream</code> predicate，以及一两条代表性日志。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">log stream --style compact --predicate 'subsystem == \"com.example.app\" &amp;&amp; category == \"Sidebar\"'\n</code></pre> <p>如果预期事件没有出现，请让 Codex 把日志移到最可能相关的控件路径附近，重新运行同一流程，并继续迭代，直到日志能解释实际情况。如果问题转向崩溃或回溯分析，就转用插件的构建/运行调试工作流，同时让遥测继续聚焦于操作边界。</p> <p><a id=\"save-a-session-trace-for-a-later-codex-pass\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex_1\">保存会话跟踪，供后续 Codex 轮次使用</h2> <p>对于耗时较长或偶发的问题，可以要求 Codex 保存经过筛选的日志流、总结时间线，并将小型跟踪文件留在本地工作区。这样后续 Codex 轮次无需只凭记忆重放整个流程，也能检查同一份证据。多轮任务中还可以比较修复前后的记录。</p> <p>当需要由人来驱动一部分流程时，这种方式同样适用：让 Codex 启动便于记录日志的调试循环，开始捕获经过筛选的日志流；必要时你手动复现，再由 Codex 读取已保存的记录。</p> <p><a id=\"practical-tips\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">实用建议</h2> <p><a id=\"instrument-one-feature-at-a-time\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">一次只埋点一个功能</h3> <p>从一个侧边栏、窗口、命令或同步路径开始，这样日志序列会更容易检查。如果该路径已经可靠，再将同一种模式扩展到相邻流程。</p> <p><a id=\"make-privacy-part-of-the-prompt\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">在提示词中考虑隐私</h3> <p>让 Codex 解释每个被记录的标识符，并避免把机密、个人数据或原始内容写入统一日志。通常只需少量事件就足以用于本地调试。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-sample-output-in-the-final-summary\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_11\">在最终摘要中保留样例输出</h3> <p>提供代表性日志行和筛选条件，比只说“已添加遥测”更有助于建立信任。还应附上简短操作时间线，便于后续 Codex 轮次复用这套验证流程。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"add-mac-telemetry\">Add Mac telemetry</h1> <p>Use Codex to instrument one Mac feature with Logger, run the app, and verify the action from unified logs.</p> <p>Use Codex and the Build macOS Apps plugin to add a few high-signal <code>Logger</code> events around windows, sidebars, commands, or sync flows, then run the app and prove from Console or <code>log stream</code> that the right actions fired.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Mac app features where Codex needs a reliable trace of window opening, sidebar selection, menu commands, menu bar actions, sync milestones, or fallback paths</li> <li>Agentic debugging loops where Codex should patch code, rerun the app, inspect logs, and decide the next fix from evidence instead of guessing</li> <li>Local app-session collection loops where you want a compact sequence of user actions and app lifecycle events that can be compared across repeated runs</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-macos-apps (online)</a></td> <td>Use the macOS telemetry and build/run skills to add structured <code>OSLog</code> instrumentation, launch the app, exercise the UI path, and verify the emitted events from Console or <code>log stream</code>.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>App logging</td> <td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/os/logger\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OSLog Logger (online)</a></td> <td>Structured unified logging gives Codex a narrow, filterable feedback loop without turning the codebase into a wall of <code>print</code> statements.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Agent workflow</td> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build macOS Apps plugin (online)</a></td> <td>The plugin's telemetry and build/run skills are designed to work together: instrument one flow, launch the app, inspect logs, and tighten the event set.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Runtime verification</td> <td>Console.app and <code>log stream --predicate ...</code></td> <td>A concrete log filter plus sample output gives the agent a repeatable handoff and makes the new instrumentation easy to verify across runs.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Instrument One Feature and Verify It from Logs</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the Build macOS Apps plugin to add lightweight unified logging around [name one Mac feature or action flow], then run the app and verify from logs that those events fire in the expected order.\n\nConstraints:\n- Prefer `Logger` from `OSLog`, not `print`, and create a clear subsystem/category pair for this feature so the logs are easy to filter.\n- Log one concise line for each important action boundary or state transition: for example window opened, sidebar selection changed, menu command invoked, sync started, sync finished, or fallback path taken.\n- Keep permanent `info` logs stable and high signal. Use `debug` only for noisy local details, and remove or demote temporary instrumentation before finishing.\n- Do not log secrets, auth tokens, personal data, or raw document contents. If an identifier must be logged, choose the safest privacy annotation and explain why.\n- Build and run the app, exercise the feature path yourself, and verify the events with Console or a focused `log stream` predicate.\n- If the flow is long, intermittent, or easier to reproduce by hand, save the filtered log stream to a small local session trace file, let me manually exercise the app if needed, then read that file back and summarize the event timeline.\n- If an expected event does not appear, move the log closer to the suspected control path, rerun the flow, and continue until the logs explain what happened.\n\nDeliver:\n- the new logger setup and the exact events you added\n- the Console filter or `log stream` predicate you used\n- a short before/after summary of what the logs now make observable\n- the saved trace file and timeline summary if this became a longer capture session\n- one or two representative log lines that prove the flow is instrumented correctly\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build macOS Apps plugin (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"add-one-logger-where-debugging-gets-vague\">Add one Logger where debugging gets vague</h2> <p>This use case is for Mac app flows where \"something happened\" is too fuzzy to debug from code review alone. Ask Codex to add a few high-signal unified logs around one behavior, run the app, trigger that behavior, and verify from Console or <code>log stream</code> that the expected events fired.</p> <p>Use the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build macOS Apps plugin (online)</a> for that loop. Its macOS telemetry skill is intentionally lightweight: use Apple's <code>Logger</code>, choose a clear subsystem/category pair, log action boundaries and state transitions, avoid sensitive payloads, and verify the event after a local build/run instead of assuming the instrumentation is wired correctly.</p> <h2 id=\"why-telemetry-is-useful-for-agentic-engineering\">Why telemetry is useful for agentic engineering</h2> <p>Good logs give Codex a repeatable feedback loop after each patch. Instead of asking you to manually inspect every window, menu action, or sync transition, the agent can run the app, exercise the flow, inspect filtered logs, and decide the next code change from evidence.</p> <p>That is especially useful for three agentic loops:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Hands-free debug loop:</strong> Codex instruments a suspicious flow, launches the app, clicks the sidebar or triggers a command, reads the emitted log sequence, patches the state update path, and reruns the same flow until the logs and UI behavior agree.</li> <li><strong>App session collection loop:</strong> Codex adds one event for app launch, window open, sidebar selection, import started, import finished, and import failed, then runs a local session and summarizes the resulting timeline so missing or out-of-order transitions become obvious.</li> <li><strong>Human-driven capture loop:</strong> Codex launches the app with logging enabled, keeps a focused log stream running while you manually exercise a tricky flow, then inspects the captured session afterward and proposes the next patch from that trace.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"keep-the-instrumentation-small-and-filterable\">Keep the instrumentation small and filterable</h2> <p>Ask Codex for one logger per feature area, not one permanent log line for every state mutation. Feature categories such as <code>Windowing</code>, <code>Commands</code>, <code>MenuBar</code>, <code>Sidebar</code>, <code>Sync</code>, or <code>Import</code> make logs much easier to filter during the next debugging pass.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-swift\">import OSLog\n\nprivate let logger = Logger(\n  subsystem: Bundle.main.bundleIdentifier ?? \"SampleApp\",\n  category: \"Sidebar\"\n)\n\n@MainActor\nfunc selectItem(_ item: SidebarItem) {\n  logger.info(\"Selected sidebar item: \\(item.id, privacy: .public)\")\n  selection = item.id\n}\n</code></pre> <p>Use <code>info</code> for concise action and lifecycle events that should remain useful over time, and <code>debug</code> for noisier local state details that may be removed or demoted before the task is done. Add signposts only when you are measuring a timing span, not by default.</p> <h2 id=\"ask-codex-to-prove-the-event-from-logs\">Ask Codex to prove the event from logs</h2> <p>The useful part is not just adding <code>Logger</code> calls. Ask Codex to run the app, trigger the instrumented flow, and give you the exact Console filter or <code>log stream</code> predicate it used plus one or two representative log lines.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">log stream --style compact --predicate 'subsystem == \"com.example.app\" &amp;&amp; category == \"Sidebar\"'\n</code></pre> <p>If an expected event does not appear, ask Codex to move the log closer to the suspected control path, rerun the same flow, and keep iterating until the logs explain what happened. If the task turns into a crash or backtrace analysis, pivot to the plugin's build/run debugging workflow and keep the telemetry focused on the action boundaries.</p> <h2 id=\"save-a-session-trace-for-a-later-codex-pass\">Save a session trace for a later Codex pass</h2> <p>For longer or intermittent bugs, ask Codex to save a focused log stream to a small local trace file, summarize the timeline, and leave that artifact in the workspace so a later Codex run can inspect the same evidence without replaying the whole session from memory. That makes multi-pass debugging easier when you want one agent run to collect a trace and another run to compare behavior before and after a patch.</p> <p>This also works well when the human needs to drive part of the session. Ask Codex to launch the app in a logging-friendly debug loop, start a filtered capture, wait while you reproduce the issue manually, and then read the saved trace file once you are done.</p> <h2 id=\"practical-tips\">Practical tips</h2> <h3 id=\"instrument-one-feature-at-a-time\">Instrument one feature at a time</h3> <p>Start with one sidebar, window, command, or sync path so the log sequence stays easy to inspect. If that path becomes reliable, Codex can expand the same pattern to neighboring flows.</p> <h3 id=\"make-privacy-part-of-the-prompt\">Make privacy part of the prompt</h3> <p>Ask Codex to explain every logged identifier and to avoid writing secrets, personal data, or raw content to unified logs. A tiny event vocabulary is usually enough for local debugging.</p> <h3 id=\"keep-sample-output-in-the-final-summary\">Keep sample output in the final summary</h3> <p>Representative log lines make the change much easier to trust than \"telemetry was added.\" Ask Codex to include the filter predicate and a short action timeline so the next agent run can reuse the same verification loop.</p>"};
